  "body": "## What changed\n\nA tilted (3+1 / 3+2, `tilt.a_deg`/`b_deg`) operation took its reference heights - Top/Bottom of stock, Top/Bottom of model, Work offset - as the setup's world Z and only subtracted the plane origin's Z. It never measured along the turned tool axis. On #2389's bar (10 Y x 30 Z, centred on A) a Slot at A 90 with Top = Top of stock got 15 along the axis instead of 5, so it cut air. On other sides of an asymmetric stock it would plunge to the wrong depth.\n\n- New `camcraft_app::operation::fold_height` (`crates/app/src/operation/tilt_heights.rs`). Under a non-upright tilt, each reference height is the referenced geometry's extent along the tool axis (`TiltedFrame::z_local` over its facets). It is returned as `z_local + origin.z`, so the existing `- origin.z` fold in `run_job` / `source_region` gives exactly the local value.\n- Where it is used: the generation heights (`collect_job` through `resolve_params_folded`), the Contour/Pocket/Trace section plane (`section_z_of`) and the area-controls cut plane (`boundary_ctx`).\n- Unchanged: Fixed heights keep the shipped `h - origin.z` law (pinned by `tilt.rs`). A Selection reference keeps the setup resolve, because a tilted op refuses a picked source first. Untilted ops and upright tilts (A0 B0) read the setup resolve verbatim, so prismatic paths and goldens keep their bits.\n- `resolve_params` now delegates to `resolve_params_with` (the resolver is passed in). The refusal wording is unchanged.\n- The viewport planes and the Heights tab's \"(= Z ...)\" echo are display-only and were split out to #2416 (P3, filed). Decision record: `docs/decisions/2389-tilt-heights-axis.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests, in the new file `crates/app/tests/tilt_heights.rs`:\n- `a_slot_at_a90_reads_top_of_stock_along_the_tool_axis`: the issue's proof. Clearance along the axis is 15 (main gives 25) and the bottom is 4.\n- `an_offset_bar_reads_its_own_side_at_a_minus_90_and_the_underside`: an asymmetric stock (Y -1..11, Z -20..10) with a plane origin off the world origin.\n  - A -90, origin (2,0,3): top 11; clearance 21 along the axis (main gives 17).\n  - A0 B180, origin Z 3: top 23. This case also exercises the `+ origin.z` hand-off.\n- `a_tilted_contour_sections_the_model_along_the_tool_axis`: a tilted Contour on a part, with Top/Bottom of model. On main it is refused with \"no material at z = 14.000\"; with the fix it contours at local 4..3.\n\nMutation check (revert, then restore):\n- `collect_job` set back to the setup resolve: tests 1 and 2 go red (25 vs 15; 17 vs 21).\n- `section_z_of` given no frame: test 3 goes red.\n- `+ origin.z` dropped from `fold_height`: test 2 goes red (18 vs 21).\n- With everything restored, all three are green.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 247 steps, 0 failed (14.6 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. It includes `first_4axis_part`, which holds `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` and `.nc` byte-for-byte (the round bar is symmetric about A, so it stays unchanged), plus `tilt`, `tilt_basis_compat`, `opframe_seam` and the heights suites.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI planes and echo (#2416).\n- The post's `ClearancePlane` parameter for a tilted op still states the setup Z (`posting.rs`).\n- `material_local.top` is still `material.top - origin.z`.\n- A tilt at a non-right angle (e.g. A 45) on a round bar: the facet extent is the tessellation's, which can be up to one chord sagitta under the true cylinder.\n- Bore/Thread under a tilt: they read the same height set, but no test covers them.\n- No machine run.\n\nChangelog: A tilted (3+2) operation now measures Top/Bottom of stock, Top/Bottom of model and Work offset heights along its tool axis, not as the setup's Z (#2389)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #2389 (the viewport planes and \"(= Z ...)\" text, #2416, finish it)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
